{
  "caseId": "averitec-dev-0208",
  "atoms": [
    {
      "id": "atom-1",
      "text": "It makes no sense for oil to be cheaper in Nigeria than in Saudi Arabia.",
      "sourceText": "It makes no sense for oil to be cheaper in Nigeria than in Saudi Arabia.",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 72
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "atomId": "atom-1",
      "spans": [
        {
          "id": "doc-07b5051e0f4b::sentence-72",
          "documentId": "doc-07b5051e0f4b",
          "text": "No export or import prices are necessary. ",
          "start": 8549,
          "end": 8591
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-4480543c9460::sentence-24",
          "documentId": "doc-4480543c9460",
          "text": "GDP per capita in Nigeria and other countries is calculated as the Gross Domestic Product (GDP) divided by the population.\n",
          "start": 890,
          "end": 1013
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-07b5051e0f4b::sentence-32",
          "documentId": "doc-07b5051e0f4b",
          "text": "But in a world where trade occurs, prices that are made up of commodities produced need not correspond to the prices of commodities consumed.\n",
          "start": 2744,
          "end": 2886
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-4480543c9460::sentence-15",
          "documentId": "doc-4480543c9460",
          "text": "Historically, the average for Nigeria from 1990 to 2024 is 6754 U.S. dollars. ",
          "start": 486,
          "end": 564
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-4480543c9460::sentence-1",
          "documentId": "doc-4480543c9460",
          "text": "Nigeria: GDP per capita, PPP\n",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 29
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-07b5051e0f4b::sentence-113",
          "documentId": "doc-07b5051e0f4b",
          "text": "The OECD then requires producing power deflators, not purchasing power deflators. ",
          "start": 15158,
          "end": 15240
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
